rules.body:
In the following table is given a complete classification of these letters according to the organs with which they are pronounced.

(a) The organs of pronunciation are the five parts situated in the mouth, viz, the throat, the palate, the roof or upper part of the palate, the teeth and the lips.

**Note:** In the following table the nether stroke (see @ref[10] below) is omitted. It should be supposed to be present.

|                  | Unaspirate | Aspirate | Unaspirate | Aspirate | Nasals | Semivowels | Sibilants | Simple vowels | Diphthongs |
|------------------|------------|----------|------------|----------|--------|------------|-----------|---------------|------------|
| **Gutturals**    | @deva[क]   | @deva[ख] | @deva[ग]   | @deva[घ] | @deva[ङ] | @deva[ह][^1] | @deva[ᳵ] Jiv. | @deva[अ], @deva[आ] | @deva[ओ], @deva[औ] |
| **Palatals**     | @deva[च]   | @deva[छ] | @deva[ज]   | @deva[झ] | @deva[ञ] | @deva[य]   | @deva[श]  | @deva[इ], @deva[ई] | @deva[ए], @deva[ऐ] |
| **Linguals**     | @deva[ट]   | @deva[ठ] | @deva[ड]   | @deva[ढ] | @deva[ण] | @deva[र]   | @deva[ष]  | @deva[ऋ], @deva[ॠ] | |
| **Dentals**      | @deva[त]   | @deva[थ] | @deva[द]   | @deva[ध] | @deva[न] | @deva[ल]   | @deva[स]  | @deva[ऌ] | |
| **Labials**      | @deva[प]   | @deva[फ] | @deva[ब]   | @deva[भ] | @deva[म] | @deva[व]   | @deva[ᳶ] Upa. | @deva[उ], @deva[ऊ] | @deva[ओ], @deva[औ] |

This can be more easily remembered from its Sanskrit form which is as follows:—

@deva[अकुहविसर्जनीयां कण्ठः ।]
@deva[इचुयशानां तालु ।]
@deva[ऋटुरषाणां मूर्धा ।]
@deva[ऌतुलसानां दन्ताः ।]
@deva[उपूपध्मानीयानां ओष्ठौ ।]
@deva[अमङणनानां नासका च ।]

@deva[एदैतोः कण्ठतालु ।]
@deva[ओदौतोः कण्ठौष्ठम् ।]
@deva[वकारस्य दन्तौष्ठम् ।]
@deva[जिह्वामूलीयस्य जिह्वामूलम् ।]
@deva[नासिकाऽनुस्वारस्य ।]

The linguals are called cerebrals in some European Grammars. @deva[ए] and @deva[ऐ] are both guttural and palatal; @deva[ओ] and @deva[औ] are guttural and labial; @deva[व] is dental and labial. The nose is the organ of pronunciation of the Anusvāra, while the root of the tongue is that of the Jihvāmūlīya.

---

[^1]: @deva[ह] though not a semivowel is put here as it is a guttural.

The forms which the vowel signs assume when added to consonants and the changes which some letters undergo when compounded are given below, under (a) and (b).

**(a)** @deva[अ] added to a consonant is denoted by the removal of the nether stroke; as @deva[क्] + @deva[अ] = @deva[क] @[ka]. The remaining vowels when compounded with a consonant become, @deva[ा], @deva[ि], @deva[ी], @deva[ु], @deva[ू], @deva[ृ], @deva[ॄ], @deva[ॢ], @deva[े], @deva[ै], @deva[ो], @deva[ौ], respectively; as @deva[क्] + @deva[आ] = @deva[का] @[kā], @deva[क्] + @deva[इ] = @deva[कि] @[ki]; similarly @deva[की] @[kī], @deva[कु] @[ku], @deva[कू] @[kū], @deva[कृ] @[kṛ], @deva[कॄ] @[kṝ], @deva[कॢ] @[kḷ], @deva[के] @[ke], @deva[कै] @[kai], @deva[को] @[ko], @deva[कौ] @[kau].

**Exception:** @deva[ऋ] when following upon @deva[र] remains unchanged, as @deva[रृ].

**(b)** In compounding consonants they should be taken in the order in which they are pronounced; the last consonant takes a vowel, the preceding ones generally losing their nether and perpendicular strokes when combined e.g. tsna ought to be written as @deva[त्स्न], ṇṇa as @deva[ण्ण], &c. Some letters, however, change their form slightly and others entirely, when compounded with other consonants; e.g. @deva[ल्प] @[lpa]; @deva[त्र] @[tra]; @deva[श्च] @[śca]; @deva[ग्र] @[gra], &c.; @deva[र] immediately preceding another consonant (or the vowel @deva[ऋ]) is denoted by the sign @deva[र्] written above the following consonant as @deva[र्क] @[rka]. It is then necessarily called a @deva[रेफ].

**(c)** In the conjuncts @deva[क्ष] (@deva[क्] + @deva[ष्]) @[ksh], and @deva[ज्ञ] (@deva[ज्] + @deva[ञ्]) @[jña], the component elements are scarcely discernible.

**(d)** A few consonants are written in two ways; e.g. @deva[त्र], @deva[त्र] @[tra]; @deva[क्र], @deva[क्र] @[kra]; @deva[स्थ], @deva[स्थ] @[stha]; @deva[क्त], @deva[क्त] @[kta]; @deva[स्त्र], @deva[स्त्र] @[stra].

**(e)** The following are the principal conjunct consonants:

@deva[क्क] @[k-ka], @deva[क्कण] @[k-kṇa], @deva[क्क्य] @[k-kya], @deva[क्ख] @[k-kha], @deva[क्त] @[k-ta], @deva[क्थ] @[k-tha], @deva[क्त्य] @[k-tya], @deva[क्त्र] or @deva[क्र] @[k-tra], @deva[क्त्व] @[k-tva], @deva[क्थ्न] @[k-thna], @deva[क्न] @[k-na], @deva[क्न्य] @[k-nya], @deva[क्म] @[k-ma], @deva[क्य] @[k-ya], @deva[क्र] or @deva[क्र] @[k-ra], @deva[क्ल] @[k-la], @deva[क्व] @[k-va], @deva[क्ष] @[k-ṣa], @deva[क्ष्ण] @[k-ṣ-ṇa], @deva[क्ष्म] @[k-ṣ-ma], @deva[क्ष्य] @[k-ṣ-ya], @deva[क्ष्व] @[k-ṣ-va].

@deva[ख्न] @[kh-na], @deva[ख्य] @[kh-ya], @deva[ख्र] @[kh-ra].

@deva[ग्ध] @[g-dha], @deva[ग्न] @[g-na], @deva[ग्य] @[g-ya], @deva[ग्र] @[g-ra], @deva[ग्र्य] @[g-rya], @deva[ग्ल] @[g-la], @deva[ग्व] @[g-va], @deva[घ्न] @[gh-na], @deva[घ्न्य] @[gh-nya], @deva[घ्म] @[gh-ma], @deva[घ्य] @[gh-ya], @deva[घ्र] @[gh-ra], @deva[घ्व] @[gh-va].

@deva[ङ्क] @[ṅ-ka], @deva[ङ्क्त] @[ṅ-kta], @deva[ङ्क्ष] @[ṅ-k-ṣa], @deva[ङ्क्ष्व] @[ṅ-k-ṣ-va], @deva[ङ्ख] @[ṅ-kha], @deva[ङ्ख्य] @[ṅ-kh-ya], @deva[ङ्ग] @[ṅ-ga], @deva[ङ्घ] @[ṅ-gha], @deva[ङ्घ्य] @[ṅ-gh-ya], @deva[ङ्घ्र] @[ṅ-gh-ra], @deva[ङ्न] @[ṅ-na], @deva[ङ्म] @[ṅ-ma], @deva[ङ्य] @[ṅ-ya].

@deva[च्च] @[c-ca], @deva[च्छ] @[c-cha], @deva[च्छ्र] @[c-ch-ra], @deva[च्छ्व] @[c-ch-va], @deva[च्ञ] @[c-ña], @deva[च्म] @[c-ma], @deva[च्य] @[c-ya].

@deva[छ्य] @[ch-ya], @deva[छ्र] @[ch-ra].

@deva[ज्ज] @[j-ja], @deva[ज्झ] @[j-jha], @deva[ज्ञ] @[j-ña], @deva[ज्ञ्य] @[j-ñ-ya], @deva[ज्म] @[j-ma], @deva[ज्य] @[j-ya], @deva[ज्र] @[j-ra], @deva[ज्व] @[j-va].

@deva[ञ्च] @[ñ-ca], @deva[ञ्छ] @[ñ-cha], @deva[ञ्ज] @[ñ-ja].

