|---|---|
| @deva[अद्] (2 cl.) @deva[अदत्] eating. | @deva[रुध्] (7 cl.) @deva[रुन्धत्] preventing. |
| @deva[या] (2 cl.) @deva[यात्] going | @deva[कृ] (8 cl.) @deva[कुर्वत्] doing. |
| @deva[हु] (3 cl.) @deva[जुह्वत्] sacrificing | @deva[तन्] (8 cl.) @deva[तन्वत्] stretching, &c. |
| @deva[दिव्] (4 cl.) @deva[दीव्यत्] playing. | @deva[क्री] (9 cl.) @deva[क्रीणत्] buying. |
| @deva[सु] (5 cl.) @deva[सुन्वत्] extracting. | @deva[मुष्] (9 cl.) @deva[मुष्णत्] stealing, &c. |
| @deva[तुद्] (6 cl.) @deva[तुदत्] giving pain. | @deva[चुर्] (10 cl.) @deva[चोरयत्] stealing. |

@deva[बोधय्] cau. of @deva[बुध्], @deva[बोधयत्] causing to know.

@deva[बुबोधिष्] desid. of @deva[बुध्], @deva[बुबोधिषत्] desiring to know.

@deva[दित्स्] desid. of @deva[दा], @deva[दित्सत्] desiring to give.

@deva[चेक्षिप्] freq. of @deva[क्षिप्], @deva[चेक्षिपत्] throwing again and again.

&c. &c. &c. &c. &c.

(a) The term. @deva[अत्] is optionally changed to @deva[वस्] when added to the root @deva[विद्]; @deva[विद्वत्] or @deva[विद्वस्] 'knowing.'

(b) The affix @deva[अत्] when added to @deva[द्विष्] and @deva[सु] 'to extract Soma juice in a sacrifice' has the sense of an agent; as @deva[द्विषत्] *m.* 'an enemy.' @deva[यज्ञे सर्वे सुन्वन्तः] 'all are the extractors of Soma juice in a sacrifice.

(c) When affixed to @deva[अर्ह्] it has the sense of 'fitness, respect;' @deva[अर्हत्] 'one deserving respect, respectable.'

(d) @deva[इ] 2 P. and @deva[धृ] cau. take the affix @deva[अत्] when the idea of difficulty is not present; @deva[अधीयत्] 'studying without experiencing any difficulty;' @deva[धारयत्] 'holding or bearing with ease;' but @deva[कृच्छ्रेण अधीते], @deva[कृच्छ्रेण धारयति].

**By means of the affix @deva[ण्यत्].**

Roots ending in @deva[ऋ], and those ending in a consonant take the affix @deva[ण्यत्] (@deva[य]) in the same sense as @deva[यत्]. Before this affix the ending @deva[च्] and @deva[ज्] of a root are changed to @deva[क्] and @deva[ग्] respectively and the final vowel and the penultimate @deva[अ] take Vṛiddhi substitute; any other penultimate vowel generally takes Guṇa.

@deva[कृ]—@deva[कार्यं] 'what ought to be done,' @deva[धृ]—@deva[धार्यं] 'what ought to be worn,' &c.; @deva[ग्रह्]—@deva[ग्राह्यं], @deva[दभ्]—@deva[दाभ्यं] 'what ought to be impelled,' &c.; @deva[वच्]—@deva[वाक्यं] 'what is arranged, a sentence,' @deva[पच्]—@deva[पाक्यं] 'what is to be cooked,' @deva[मृज्]—@deva[मार्ग्यं] 'what is to be purified,' &c.

In the following list are alphabetically arranged almost all the common Kṛt affixes forming nouns (substantive and adjective) with various significations from roots or derivative bases. @deva[अ]—(@deva[अच्], @deva[अण्], @deva[अप्], @deva[कञ्], @deva[खच्], @deva[खश्], @deva[खल्], @deva[घ], @deva[घञ्], @deva[ट], @deva[टक्], @deva[ड], @deva[ण], and @deva[श]):—

@deva[अच्]—denoting 'the agent' is added to—@deva[पच्] and other roots; @deva[पचतीति पचः] 'one who cooks;' @deva[चर्]—@deva[चरः], @deva[चुर्]—@deva[चोरः], @deva[भू]—@deva[भवः], @deva[नद्]—@deva[नदः] (@deva[नदी]);—to @deva[भृ] and @deva[पच्], when the words @deva[जार] and @deva[श्वन्] are prefixed to them respectively; @deva[जारभरा] 'an adulteress;' @deva[श्वपचः] 'a Chāndāla'—to @deva[हृ] when the noun governed by it is used prepositionally and when the idea of difficulty is not present or when the whole compound denotes 'age;' @deva[अंशं हरतीति अंशहरः] 'one entitled to a share, a heir'; but @deva[भारहारः] 'a load-bearer' (@deva[भार+हृ+अण्]); @deva[कवलहरः] 'a young child;' also when @deva[आ] is prefixed to it in the sense of 'in the habit of.' @deva[पुष्पाणि हर्तुं शीलमस्य असौ पुष्पहरः];—to the root @deva[ग्रह्] when the words @deva[शक्ति] 'a missile,' @deva[लाङ्गल] 'a plough,' @deva[अङ्कुश] 'an iron hook,' @deva[तोमर] 'a javelin,' @deva[यष्टि] 'a stick,' @deva[घट], @deva[घटी] and @deva[धनुष्] are prefixed to it; @deva[शक्तिं गृह्णातीति शक्तिग्रहः] 'one armed with a spear,' &c; @deva[लाङ्गलग्रहः] &c.; also when @deva[सूत्र] is prefixed to it and the root is used in the sense of 'wearing'; @deva[सूत्रग्रहः] 'wearing a sacred thread;' but @deva[सूत्रग्राहः] (@deva[सूत्र+ग्रह्+अण्]) 'one who takes in his hand a sacred thread;'—to @deva[अर्ह्] when a noun used objectively is prefixed to it; @deva[पूजामर्हतीति पूजार्हो ब्राह्मणः] 'a Brāhmaṇa deserving worship;'—to @deva[रम्] and @deva[जप्] when the words @deva[स्तम्ब] and @deva[कर्ण] in the Loc. are prefixed to them respectively; @deva[स्तम्बेरमः] 'an elephant,' @deva[कर्णेजपः] 'one who whispers into the ear, a spy;'—to any root when the word @deva[शं] is prefixed, @deva[शंकरः], @deva[शंभवः], @deva[शंवदः] &c.,—to @deva[शी] when a word showing the place of action precedes, @deva[खे शेते] @deva[ख-(खे)शयः] 'dwelling in the sky,' so @deva[हृच्छयः] 'dwelling in the heart, i. e Madana'; also when words like @deva[पार्श्व], @deva[उदर], @deva[पृष्ठ], &c. and @deva[उत्तान], &c. precede, @deva[पार्श्व—उदर—पृष्ठ—शयः] 'sleeping on the sides,' &c., @deva[उत्तानशयः] 'lying on the back with the face upwards.' so @deva[अवमूर्धशयः] (@deva[अवनतो मूर्धा अस्य तथा शेते]) i. e. 'with the face downwards.' When added to roots ending in @deva[इ] and to some others it forms abstract nouns, @deva[चि]—@deva[चयः] 'a collection,' @deva[जि]—@deva[जयः], @deva[भी]—@deva[भयं], @deva[वृष्]—@deva[वर्षः] 'a shower of rain.' &c.

@deva[अण्]—is added to roots when the words forming their objects are prefixed to them, @deva[कुंभकारः] 'a potter,' @deva[भारहारः]—When a subanta is prefixed to @deva[हन्] with @deva[सम्], the @deva[न्] of this root is changed to @deva[ट्] optionally; @deva[वर्णसंघातः] or-@deva[टः] 'a collection of words.'

@deva[अप्]—is added to roots ending in @deva[उ] and @deva[ऋ] short or long; it sometimes forms abstract nouns, sometimes shows the place or the instrument of action denoted by the root; @deva[स्तु]—@deva[स्तवः] praise, @deva[यु]—@deva[यवः] barley, @deva[पू]—@deva[पवः], @deva[भू]—@deva[भवः], @deva[कृ]—@deva[करः] the instrument of doing anything i. e. the hand, @deva[गृ]—@deva[गरः] poison, @deva[दृ]—@deva[दरः] fear, @deva[वृ]—@deva[वरः] a boon &c., @deva[स्तृ] with @deva[वि]—@deva[विष्टरः] a tree or a seat, @deva[विस्तरः] otherwise; @deva[हन्] with @deva[सम्] takes this affix; @deva[संघः] a collection; @deva[गम्] also takes it, @deva[गमः] : @deva[अद्] preceded by a preposition takes this affix and is changed to @deva[घस्]; @deva[निघसः], @deva[प्रघसः], @deva[विघसः] &c ; food or eating; (when no preposition precedes it takes @deva[घञ्]—@deva[घासः]); the roots @deva[जप्] and @deva[व्यध्] not preceded by a preposition take @deva[अप्]: @deva[जपः] muttering prayers, @deva[व्यधः] the act of piercing; (but when a preposition precedes, they take @deva[घञ्]; as @deva[उपजापः] secret whispering into the ear, separation, &c.); the roots @deva[स्वन्] and @deva[हस्] by themselves take @deva[अप्] or @deva[घञ्]; @deva[स्वन्]—@deva[स्वनः] or @deva[स्वानः] sound; @deva[हस्]—@deva[हसः] or @deva[हासः]; with a preposition they take the latter only; @deva[प्रस्वानः]; @deva[प्रहासः] &c.; @deva[यम्] without any preposition or with the preposition @deva[उप], @deva[नि], @deva[वि] and @deva[सम्] takes either @deva[अप्] or @deva[घञ्]; @deva[यमः] or @deva[यामः] restraint, control, &c, @deva[उपयमः] or @deva[यामः] marriage; similarly @deva[नियमः] or @deva[नियामः] &c.; the roots @deva[गद्], @deva[नद्], @deva[पद्] and @deva[स्वन्], with @deva[नि] take @deva[अप्] or @deva[घञ्]; @deva[निगदः] or @deva[निगादः] speech, @deva[निनदः] or @deva[निनादः] sound, &c @deva[क्वण्] with or without @deva[नि] takes @deva[अप्] or @deva[घञ्]; @deva[क्वणः] or @deva[क्वाणः], @deva[निक्वणः] or-@deva[क्वाणः] the sound of a lute; the root @deva[मद्] when a word other than a preposition is prefixed to it takes @deva[अप्]; with a preposition it takes @deva[घञ्]; @deva[धनमदः] the pride of wealth, @deva[उन्मादः] madness, insanity; but when preceded by @deva[प्र] or @deva[सम्] it takes @deva[अप्] when the meaning is joy; @deva[प्रमदः] or @deva[संमदः]; in other cases it takes @deva[घञ्]; @deva[प्रमादः], @deva[संमादः] carelessness, oversight, a blunder. The affixes @deva[अप्] and @deva[घञ्] are added to several other roots too numerous to note here; the difference between these is that @deva[घञ्] occasions Vṛddhi of the preceding vowel, @deva[अप्] does not

@deva[क]—is added to roots having @deva[इ], @deva[उ], @deva[ऋ], or @deva[ऌ] for their penultimate, and to the roots @deva[प्री] and @deva[कृ] and denotes the agent; @deva[लिख्]—@deva[लिखः] one who writes, @deva[क्षिप्]—@deva[क्षिपः] one who throws, @deva[बुध्]—@deva[बुधः] &c. @deva[प्री]—@deva[प्रियः] one who pleases; @deva[कृ]—@deva[किरः] one who scatters; it is also added to roots ending in @deva[आ] with or without any preposition, the final @deva[आ] being dropped; @deva[ज्ञा]—@deva[ज्ञः] or @deva[प्रज्ञः] one who knows, wise; @deva[ह्वे]—@deva[ह्वः] or @deva[आह्वः] one who calls; also when a subanta is used prepositionally with it; @deva[दा]—@deva[गोदः] one who gives cows or cuts the hair; @deva[पा]—@deva[द्विपः] (@deva[द्वाभ्यां पिबतीति]) an elephant; when added to @deva[स्था] it has various meanings; @deva[समस्थः] happy, @deva[विषमस्थः] placed in difficulties; @deva[प्रस्थः] a measure of corn, &c. This is also added to @deva[ग्रह्]—@deva[गृहं] a house, @deva[गृहाः] a wife, a house.

@deva[कञ्]—is added to @deva[दृश्] not meaning 'to see' when a pronoun precedes it; @deva[तद्+दृश्=अ=तादृशः] like that; also when the words @deva[समान] and @deva[अन्य] precede; @deva[सदृशः] like to, @deva[अन्यादृशः] like another. @deva[क्स] is added similarly; @deva[सदृक्षः], @deva[तादृक्षः] &c

@deva[खच्] and @deva[खश्]—Before these the @deva[अ] of the noun forming the object of the root with which it is used prepositionally inserts the syllable @deva[म्] after it. @deva[खच्] is added to the root @deva[वद्] after @deva[प्रिय] and @deva[वश]; @deva[प्रियं वदतीति प्रियंवदः] 'one who speaks sweetly;' @deva[वशंवदः] 'subject to the influence of, obedient to the will of;'—@deva[कृ] after the words @deva[क्षेम], @deva[प्रिय], @deva[मद्र], and @deva[भय]; @deva[क्षेमं]—@deva[प्रियं]-@deva[मद्रं]-@deva[करः] doing good, &c.; @deva[भयंकरः] causing fear, dreadful, @deva[अभयंकरः];—to the root @deva[गम्] after a subanta; @deva[विहङ्गमः] passing through the sky, a bird;—to the roots @deva[भृ], @deva[तृ], @deva[दृ], @deva[जि], @deva[धृ], @deva[सह्], @deva[तप्] and @deva[दम्] when the whole is a name; @deva[विश्वंभरः] God; @deva[रथंतरं] a portion of the Sāma Veda; @deva[पतिंवरा] a bride who chooses her husband; @deva[शत्रुंजयः] an elephant, @deva[युगंधरः] name of a mountain; @deva[परंतपः] name of a king; @deva[अरिंदमः] name of a king;—to @deva[यम्] after @deva[वाच्], @deva[वाचंयमः] one who restrains his speech for the observation of a vow;—to the roots @deva[सह्] and @deva[दृ] after the words @deva[सर्व] and @deva[पुर] respectively; @deva[सर्वंसहा] the earth, @deva[पुरंदरः] Indra;—to @deva[कष्] after the words @deva[सर्व], @deva[कूल], @deva[अभ्र] and @deva[करीष]; @deva[सर्वंकषः] all destroying, all powerful; also a rogue; @deva[कूलंकषा] (a river) sweeping away its banks; @deva[अभ्रंकषः] dashing against, coming in collision with the clouds as the wind; @deva[करीषंकषा] blowing away dry cowdung, as a strong wind or gale. @deva[खश्] is added to @deva[एज्] cau. as in @deva[जनमेजयः] making the people tremble with fear; name of a king,—to @deva[अज्], @deva[धे], @deva[तुद्] and @deva[हा] 'to go' after the words @deva[वात], @deva[शुनी], @deva[तिल] and @deva[शर्द्ध] flatulence; @deva[वातमजः] facing the wind, a kind of deer; @deva[शुनिंधयः] a kitten; @deva[तिलंतुदः] an oilman; and @deva[शर्द्धंजहाः] causing flatulence (@deva[माषाः]) a kind of bean;—to @deva[धे] and @deva[ध्मा] after the words @deva[स्तन] and @deva[नाडी], respectively @deva[स्तनंधयः] a baby sucking breast; @deva[नाडिं-(डीं)धमः] a goldsmith;—to @deva[तुद्] after @deva[विधु] and @deva[अरुष्]; @deva[विधुंतुदः] the afflictor of the moon i e. Rāhu; @deva[अरुंतुदः] (@deva[अरूंषि मर्माणि तुदतीति]) wounding the vital parts, painful;—to @deva[पच्] after words showing measure as @deva[प्रस्थंपचा स्थाली] @deva[खारिंपचः कटाहः] and after @deva[मित] and @deva[नख]-@deva[मितंपचः] one who cooks measured corn, a miser; @deva[नखंपचा] nail-scorching (as @deva[यवागूः]);—to @deva[दृश्] and @deva[तप्] after the words @deva[असूर्य] and @deva[ललाट]; @deva[असूर्यंपश्या] those who do not see the sun i e the queens of a king who are shut up in the harem; @deva[ललाटंतपः] scorching the forehead;—to @deva[दृश्], @deva[मद्] and @deva[ध्मा] after @deva[उग्र], @deva[इरम्] and @deva[पाणि] respectively; @deva[उग्रंपश्य] of a fierce aspect, @deva[इरंमदः] lightning; @deva[पाणिंधमः] a road (shrouded in such darkness that one has to clap one's hands for driving away serpents &c. that may be in the way); to @deva[मन्] meaning 'to consider oneself' as, @deva[पण्डितंमन्य], a pedant, who considers himself a Pandita; @deva[गांमन्यः] one who considers himself a cow i e. who is very humble; &c.

@deva[खल्]—is added to any root with @deva[ईषत्], @deva[दुर्] or @deva[सु] prefixed to it when the idea of ease or difficulty is present, @deva[ईषत्करः] done easily; @deva[दुष्कर] done with difficulty; @deva[सुकर] done easily, so @deva[दुःशासन], @deva[दुर्योधन], &c. &c.

@deva[घ]—is added in the sense of the place or the instrument of the action or forms abstract nouns; @deva[कृ] with @deva[आ]—@deva[आकरः] a mine; @deva[खन्] with @deva[आ], @deva[आखनः] a spade; @deva[पण्] with @deva[आ], @deva[आपणः] a place of traffic; @deva[कष्]—@deva[निकषः] a touch-stone; @deva[चर्]—@deva[गोचरः] a pasture-ground; @deva[संचरः] a path; @deva[वह्]—@deva[वहः] a shoulder; @deva[निगमः] that by which the people are guided, the Veda; @deva[व्रजः] and @deva[व्यजः] a fan. Before this @deva[छाद्] not preceded by more than one preposition becomes @deva[छद्]; @deva[दन्तच्छदः] the lip, @deva[प्रच्छदः]; but @deva[समुपच्छादः].

@deva[घञ्]—added to roots ending in consonants has almost a universal application and a variety of senses; before this the final @deva[च्] or @deva[ज्] are changed to @deva[क्] or @deva[ग्], @deva[पच्]—@deva[पाकः] food; @deva[कम्]—@deva[कामः] desire; @deva[श्रम्]—@deva[विश्रामः] rest; @deva[सृ]—@deva[सारः] strength, substance, with @deva[अति]—@deva[अतिसारः] dysentery; @deva[हृ]—@deva[हारः] a necklace, @deva[पद्]—@deva[पादः] a foot; @deva[भू]—@deva[भावः] being, a thing &c; @deva[विश्]—@deva[वेशः] a house; @deva[रुज्]—@deva[रोगः] a disease; @deva[स्पृश्]—@deva[स्पर्शः] touch; @deva[इन्ध्]—@deva[एधः] fuel; @deva[श्रन्थ्]—@deva[प्रश्रन्थः] laxity; @deva[चि]—@deva[चायः] (@deva[चीयतेऽस्मिन्नस्त्रादिकं]) the body, with @deva[नि]—@deva[निकायः] a house, &c;—to @deva[रु] when preceded by a preposition, @deva[विरावः] the warbling of birds (otherwise @deva[रवः]). The roots @deva[स्फुर्] and @deva[स्फुल्] change their vowel to @deva[आ] before this; @deva[स्फारः] or @deva[स्फालः] the throbbing of the hand, &c. @deva[रु] and @deva[प्लु] preceded by @deva[आ] take both @deva[घञ्] and @deva[अप्]; @deva[आरावः] or—@deva[रवः] a loud sound; @deva[आप्लावः]—@deva[प्लवः] a deluge. Sometimes the affixes @deva[घञ्] and @deva[अप्] are used in different senses; @deva[नी]—@deva[नायः] chief, @deva[प्रणयः] friendship, kindness; @deva[परिणायः] the act of moving a piece at chess, draughts, &c. @deva[परिणयः] marriage; @deva[इ] with @deva[नि]—@deva[न्यायः] justice, @deva[न्ययः] ruin; @deva[ग्रह्] with @deva[अव] or @deva[नि]—@deva[अवग्राहः] or @deva[निग्राहः] impediment, separation; @deva[अवग्रहः] a grammatical mark; @deva[चोरस्य निग्रहः] the confinement of a thief; but @deva[अवग्राहः]—@deva[ग्रहः] draught, want of rain; @deva[चि] after @deva[पुष्प] take the affix @deva[घञ्] when the whole means 'gathering flowers with the hands' @deva[पुष्पप्रचायः], but @deva[पुष्पचयः] 'collecting flowers with a stick' &c.; it is also added to @deva[भुज्] and @deva[उब्ज्] with @deva[नि]; @deva[भुजः] the hand; @deva[न्युब्जः] hump-backed, the Nyagrodha tree.

@deva[ट]—is added—to the root @deva[कृ] preceded by @deva[दिवा], @deva[भास्], @deva[यत्], @deva[तत्], @deva[किम्], a numeral, and nouns governed by it; @deva[दिवा करोतीति दिवाकरः], @deva[भास्करः] the sun, @deva[यत्करः] &c :—to @deva[सृ] preceded by @deva[पुरः], @deva[अग्रतः], @deva[अग्रे], and @deva[पूर्वः]; @deva[पुरःसरः], @deva[अग्रतःसरः] a leader, &c; and to @deva[चर्] preceded by @deva[भिक्षा], @deva[सेना], @deva[दाय] and words showing the place of action; @deva[भिक्षाचरः] a beggar, @deva[सेनाचरः] a soldier, &c.

@deva[टक्]—is affixed to @deva[हन्] preceded by @deva[जाया] or @deva[पति], @deva[हन्] changing to @deva[घ्न] the whole meaning 'bearing an inauspicious mark'; a husband causing the death of his wife—@deva[जायाघ्नः] bearing a mark on his body indicative of the death of his wife, similarly @deva[पतिघ्नी];—this is also added to @deva[हन्] when the agent of the action is not a man; @deva[पित्तघ्नं] checking bile, such as ghee; @deva[पतिघ्नी] (@deva[पाणिरेखा]), &c.;—to @deva[हन्] preceded by @deva[हस्तिन्] and @deva[कपाट] in the sense of 'having the power to do what is denoted by the root;' @deva[हस्तिघ्नः] 'one able to kill an elephant,' &c.;—and preceded by @deva[पाणि] and @deva[ताड] in the sense of 'one having the skill;' @deva[पाणिघः] 'one who beats time with the hand, also a drummer (beating a drum with the hand);'—to @deva[पा] 'to drink' and @deva[गै] if not preceded by a preposition; @deva[सोमपः] 'one who drinks the Soma juice'; @deva[साम गायतीति सामगः] 'one who chants the Sāma Veda'; but @deva[सामसंगायः] (when a prep. precedes it); @deva[पा] 'to protect' takes @deva[अ]; @deva[क्षीरपा ब्राह्मणी], &c.

@deva[ड]—is affixed to @deva[गम्] preceded by @deva[अन्त], @deva[अत्यन्त], @deva[अध्वन्], @deva[दूर], @deva[पार], @deva[सर्व], @deva[अनंत], @deva[सर्वत्र], @deva[पन्न] creeping on the ground,' @deva[उरस्] and @deva[विहायस्] and denotes the agent; to @deva[गम्] preceded by @deva[दुर्] and @deva[सु] and shows the place of action, before this the final consonant with the preceding vowel or the final vowel of a root is dropped; @deva[अन्तं गच्छतीति अन्तगः] 'one who goes to the end;' @deva[अध्वगः] 'a traveller;' @deva[पन्नगः], @deva[उरोगः] 'a serpent;' @deva[विहायस्] is changed to @deva[विह]—@deva[विहगः] 'a bird,' @deva[दुर्गः] 'a fortress,' &c ;—to @deva[हन्] when a blessing is implied; @deva[तव पुत्रः शत्रुहः भवेत्] 'may thy son be the destroyer of his enemies;' —also to @deva[हन्] with @deva[अप] after the words @deva[क्लेश] and @deva[तमस्]; @deva[क्लेशापहः] 'removing pain, consoling, a son;' @deva[तमोपहः] 'the dispeller of darkness, the sun,'—to @deva[जन्] preceded by a word having the sense of the Loc. or of the Ab. and not denoting a class, or when it is preceded by a preposition and the whole is a name; @deva[मंदुरजः] 'born in a stable;' @deva[सरसिजं] 'a lotus,' @deva[संस्कारजः] 'produced after some operation;' @deva[अदृष्टजः] &c ; @deva[प्रजाः], @deva[अनुजः] 'a younger brother;' the words @deva[द्विजः], @deva[अजः], @deva[ब्राह्मणजः] &c. are also formed by means of this affix; this is also added to @deva[खन्] with @deva[परि]; @deva[परिखा] 'a ditch'

@deva[ण]—is added to roots ending in @deva[आ] which insert @deva[य] before it; @deva[दा]-@deva[दायः] 'one who receives a share,' @deva[धा]—@deva[धायः] 'one who holds,' &c—to @deva[श्यै] when preceded by @deva[अव] and @deva[प्रति], @deva[अवश्यायः] 'mist, frost,' @deva[प्रतिश्यायः] 'a catarrh or cold;—to @deva[इ], @deva[स्रु], @deva[सो] and @deva[हृ] preceded by a preposition; @deva[अत्यायः] 'violation,' @deva[संस्रावः] 'oozing, trickling;' @deva[अवसायः] 'end', @deva[अवहारः] 'a thief, a seamonster';—to @deva[लिह्], @deva[श्लिष्], @deva[ग्रह्], @deva[व्यध्], @deva[श्वस्] and @deva[भू]; @deva[लेहः] 'a lambative, an electuary;' @deva[श्लेषः] 'an embrace,' @deva[ग्राहः] 'an alligator,' @deva[व्याधः] 'a hunter,' @deva[श्वासः] 'respiration,' @deva[भावः] 'a thing;—to @deva[नी] and @deva[दु] not preceded by a preposition; @deva[नायः] 'a leader', @deva[दावः] 'a forest-fire;'—to @deva[ज्वल्], @deva[चल्], @deva[जल्], @deva[टल्] 'to be confused', @deva[तल्] 'to smell,' @deva[हल्], @deva[पल्], @deva[बल्], @deva[पुल्], @deva[कुल्], @deva[शल्], @deva[हुल्], @deva[पत्], @deva[कथ्], @deva[पथ्], @deva[नथ्], @deva[वम्], @deva[भ्रम्], @deva[क्षर्], @deva[सह्], @deva[शद्], @deva[क्रुश्], @deva[बुध्], and @deva[कस्], (these may also take @deva[अच्]); @deva[ज्वालः] (or @deva[ज्वलः]), flame or blaze,' &c.—to @deva[शील्], @deva[कम्] and @deva[भक्ष्], when their objects are prefixed to them; @deva[मांसशीलः] 'one who keeps flesh;' @deva[मांसकमः] 'one who wishes for flesh,' @deva[मांसभक्षः] 'one who eats flesh';—to @deva[ईक्ष्], @deva[क्षम्] and @deva[चर्] with @deva[आ], @deva[सुखप्रतीक्षः] 'one desiring happiness,' @deva[बहुक्षमः] 'forgiving much' @deva[कल्याणाचारः] 'good-conducted;'—to @deva[ह्वे], @deva[वे] and @deva[मा] after their objects; @deva[स्वर्गे ह्वयते स्वर्गह्वायः], @deva[तन्तुवायः] 'a weaver,' @deva[धान्यमायः] 'measure of corn;'—to @deva[अद्] with @deva[नि], @deva[न्यदः] 'food.'

@deva[श]—is added to @deva[पा], @deva[घ्रा], @deva[ध्मा], @deva[धे], and @deva[दृश्]; @deva[पा]—@deva[पिबः] 'one who drinks;' @deva[घ्रा]—@deva[जिघ्रः] 'one who smells; @deva[दृश्]—@deva[पश्यः] 'one who sees;—to @deva[दा] and @deva[धा] 3 cl.; @deva[दा]—@deva[ददः] 'one who gives,' @deva[धा]—@deva[दधः] 'one who holds;—to @deva[लिम्प्] and @deva[विद्]; @deva[लिपः] 'one who plasters;' @deva[विन्दः] 'one who knows;' also when the former is preceded by @deva[नि] and the latter by @deva[गो] and other words; @deva[निलिम्पः] 'a god;' @deva[गोविन्दः] 'name of Vishṇu;' @deva[अरविन्दः] 'a lotus;'—to the Cau. of @deva[चित्], @deva[पू], @deva[एज्] with @deva[उत्], and @deva[धृ]; @deva[चेतयः] 'one who thinks or knows;' @deva[पारयः] 'one who fills'; @deva[उदेजयः] 'one who makes another tremble,' cf. Bhaṭṭi. I. 25. @deva[धारयः] 'one who holds'; added to all roots it forms abstract fem. nouns; @deva[कृ]—@deva[क्रिया] 'an act;' @deva[इष्]—@deva[इच्छा] a 'wish;' @deva[परिचर्]—@deva[परिचर्या] 'service;' @deva[मृग्]—@deva[मृगया] 'hunting;' @deva[अट्]—@deva[अटाट्या] rambling;' @deva[जागृ]—@deva[जागर्या] 'wakefulness, &c.'

@deva[अ]—forms abstract nouns from derivative bases; @deva[कृ]—@deva[चिकीर्षा] a desire to do; @deva[पुत्रकाम्या] a desire to have a son, &c. Also from roots ending in a consonant having a long vowel for their penultimate; @deva[ईह्]—@deva[ईहा] desire, @deva[ऊह्]—@deva[ऊहा] a guess; reasoning, &c.

@deva[अङ्]—similarly forms abstract nouns; it is added to roots marked with an indicatory @deva[ऋ] and to @deva[भिद्] and others; @deva[जृ]—@deva[जरा] old age; @deva[त्रप्]—@deva[त्रपा] shame, &c.; @deva[भिद्]-@deva[भिदा] distinction; separation; @deva[चित्]—@deva[चिन्ता] contemplation, anxiety; @deva[मृज्]—@deva[मृजा] cleansing &c.—to @deva[कृप्] which changes its @deva[र्] to @deva[ऌ]-@deva[कृपा] mercy; to roots ending in @deva[आ] if a preposition or the words @deva[श्रत्] and @deva[अन्तर्] precede, @deva[दा]—@deva[प्रदा] giving gift, @deva[भा]—@deva[प्रभा] lustre, &c. @deva[धा] with @deva[श्रत्]—@deva[श्रद्धा] faith; with @deva[अन्तर्]—@deva[अन्तर्धा] disappearance.

@deva[अक]—(@deva[क्वुन्], @deva[ण्वुल्], @deva[वुञ्], @deva[वुन्], @deva[ष्वुन्])—

@deva[क्वुन्]—is added to @deva[रञ्ज्]; @deva[रजकः] 'a washerman.'

@deva[ण्वुल्]—is affixed to all roots and denotes the agent of the action; @deva[कृ]—@deva[कारकः] one who makes, acting, &c.; @deva[पच्]—@deva[पाचकः] one who cooks; @deva[हन्]-@deva[घातकः] @deva[दा]—@deva[दायकः], @deva[धा]—@deva[धायकः], &c; it is added to @deva[शम्] and other roots of that group; but in this case the preceding vowel is not lengthened @deva[शम्]-@deva[शमकः], @deva[दम्]-@deva[दमकः], @deva[वधकः] a killer, @deva[जनकः] a father, &c. Added to some roots it forms the name of diseases; @deva[छर्द्]-@deva[प्रच्छर्दिका] vomiting; @deva[वह्]-@deva[प्रवाहिका] dysentery; diarrhœa; @deva[चर्च्]-@deva[विचर्चिका] itch, scab, &c; sometimes it is added to denote the meanings of roots @deva[आस्]-@deva[आसिका] sitting, @deva[शी]-@deva[शायिका] sleeping, &c.; sometimes it has the sense of futurity, @deva[कृष्णं दर्शको याति] he goes desirous of seeing Krishṇa; @deva[सतां पालकः] &c.

@deva[वुञ्]—is added to @deva[निन्द्], @deva[हिंस्], @deva[क्लिश्], @deva[खाद्]; @deva[नश्] with @deva[वि], @deva[क्षिप्] with @deva[परि], @deva[रट्], @deva[वद्], @deva[द्ये], @deva[भाष्] 'and @deva[सृ] in the sense of the 'agent,' or 'in the habit of,' @deva[निन्द्]—@deva[निन्दकः] 'one who blames or is in the habit of blaming or censuring others,' @deva[हिंस्]—@deva[हिंसकः], @deva[क्लिश्]-@deva[क्लेशकः] &c.;—to @deva[दिव्] and @deva[क्रुश्] preceded by @deva[आ]; @deva[आदेवकः] 'a gambler,' @deva[आक्रोशकः] 'one who calls out or vociferates, reviler.'

@deva[वुन्]—is added to @deva[प्रु], @deva[सृ] and @deva[लु] in the sense 'skilul in,' @deva[प्रु]—@deva[प्रवकः] @deva[सृ]—@deva[सरकः], 'skilful in walking;' @deva[लवकः] 'skilful in cutting:' this may by added to any root when the idea of a blessing is to be conveyed; @deva[जीवकस्त्वं भूयाः] 'mayest thou live for many years,' @deva[नन्दकस्त्वं भूयाः] 'mayest thou be the giver of delight.'

@deva[ष्वुन्]—is added to @deva[नृत्], @deva[खन्] and @deva[रज्] in the sense of 'one who knows the art of;' @deva[नर्तकः] 'one who knows the art of dancing;' @deva[खनकः] 'a digger,' 'a miner;' @deva[रञ्जकः] 'a dyer.'

@deva[अथु]—(@deva[अथुच्])—@deva[वेप्]-@deva[वेपथुः] 'tremor;' @deva[श्वि]—@deva[श्वयथुः] 'swelling, a tumour;' '@deva[दु]—@deva[दवथुः] 'pain, anxiety,' &c

@deva[अन]—(@deva[ण्युट्], @deva[युच्], @deva[ल्यु], @deva[ल्युट्])—

@deva[ण्युट्]—is affixed to @deva[गै] and @deva[हा]; @deva[गायनः] 'a singer;' @deva[हायनः] 'a year,' 'a kind of rice'

@deva[युच्]—is affixed to verbs meaning 'to go or to sound,' @deva[चल्]—@deva[चलनः] 'one who moves.' @deva[रु]—@deva[रवणः] 'one who makes a sound,' so @deva[शब्दनः] &c. It is also affixed to verbs meaning 'to ornament, to deck, and to be angry,'—@deva[भूष्]-@deva[भूषणः] serving as an ornament @deva[मण्ड्]-@deva[मण्डनः], @deva[क्रुध्]-@deva[क्रोधनः], @deva[रुष्]-@deva[रोषणः] angry, irascible'--to @deva[जु], @deva[सृ], @deva[गृध्], @deva[ज्वल्], @deva[शुच्], @deva[लष्], @deva[पत्], @deva[पद्]; @deva[जु]-@deva[जवनः] 'a swift walker;' @deva[सृ]-@deva[सरणः] 'one who goes' @deva[गृध्]-@deva[गर्धनः] 'a glutton;' @deva[ज्वलनः] 'that which blazes, fire;'—to some other roots ending in a consonant, @deva[वृत्]-@deva[वर्तनः], @deva[वृध्]-@deva[वर्धनः] &c.:-to the freq of @deva[क्रम्] and @deva[द्रम्], @deva[चंक्रमणः], @deva[दंद्रमणः] 'one who goes again and again', it also forms fem. abstract nouns with the causals of roots and the verbs @deva[श्रन्थ्], @deva[घट्], @deva[वन्द्] and @deva[इष्] not meaning 'to wish,' @deva[कृ]-@deva[कारणा] 'doing action,' @deva[हृ]-@deva[हारणा], @deva[आस्]—@deva[आसना], @deva[श्रन्थ्]—@deva[श्रन्थना], @deva[घट्]-@deva[घटना], @deva[वन्द्] @deva[वन्दना], @deva[विद्]-@deva[वेदना]. @deva[इष्] with @deva[अनु]-@deva[अन्वेषणा] 'searching.'

@deva[ल्यु]—is affixed to @deva[नन्द्] and other roots; @deva[नन्दनः] 'one who delights, a son,' @deva[मद्]—@deva[मदनः] 'he who exhilarates, the god of love,' @deva[साध्]-@deva[साधनः] 'one who accomplishes,' @deva[सह्]—@deva[सहनः] 'one who bears,' @deva[सूद्]—@deva[मधुसूदनः] 'the killer of Madhu,' @deva[अर्द्]—@deva[जनार्दनः] 'the chastiser of the sinful,' @deva[भी]—@deva[विभीषणः] 'terrifier, name of Rāvaṇa's brother.'

@deva[ल्युट्]—is added to all nouns to form neu. abstract nouns; @deva[सह्]—@deva[सहनं] endurance, @deva[हस्]—@deva[हसनं] laughing, @deva[शी]—@deva[शयनं] sleeping, @deva[पा]—@deva[पानं] drinking, @deva[भुज्]—@deva[भोजनं], @deva[साध्]—@deva[साधनं], &c. This is also added in the sense of 'the instrument of an action'; @deva[व्रश्च्]—@deva[व्रश्चनः] an instrument for cutting; an axe, &c; @deva[दुह्]—@deva[गोदोहनी] a milk vessel (here it shows the place of action of Adhikaraṇa).

@deva[आक]—(@deva[षाकन्])—is affixed to @deva[जल्प्], @deva[भिक्ष्], @deva[कुट्ट्], @deva[लुंठ्] and @deva[वृ] in the sense of 'in the habit of;' @deva[जल्पाकः] (@deva[जल्पितुं शीलमस्य]) 'a prattler; @deva[भिक्ष्]—@deva[भिक्षाकः] 'a beggar,' @deva[कुट्टाकः] 'he who divides or cuts;' @deva[लुंठाकः] 'a robber;' @deva[वराकः] 'a poor man.'

@deva[आरु]—@deva[शृ]—@deva[शरारु] destructive, hurtful; @deva[वंद्]—@deva[वंदारु] praising, a panegyrist.

@deva[आलु]—is added to the cau. of @deva[स्पृह्], @deva[ग्रह्] and @deva[पत्], to @deva[दय्] and to the words @deva[निद्रा], @deva[तन्द्रा] and @deva[श्रद्धा]; @deva[स्पृहयालु] longing for, desirous of; @deva[दयालु] compassionate; @deva[निद्रालु] disposed to sleep; @deva[तन्द्रालुः]; @deva[श्रद्धालुः] 'full of faith.'

@deva[इ]—(@deva[इक्], @deva[इञ्], @deva[इण्], @deva[कि])—

@deva[इक्]—@deva[कृष्]—@deva[कृषिः] 'one who tills the ground'; @deva[गृ]-@deva[गिरिः] a mountain.

@deva[इञ्]—is added to @deva[वप्] and other roots; @deva[वापिः] a well; @deva[वासिः] a dwelling.

@deva[इण्]—is added to @deva[अज्] and other roots of the group; @deva[आजिः] a battle, @deva[आतिः] &c.

@deva[कि]—is added to the roots @deva[दा] and @deva[धा] and others assuming these forms; @deva[धा]—@deva[उपाधिः] fraud, condition, &c.; @deva[निधिः] a treasure, @deva[संधिः] a joint, peace, &c.; @deva[जलधिः] the sea (here it is used in the sense of @deva[अधिकरण]).

@deva[इत्र]—(@deva[इत्रच्]) is added to @deva[ऋ], @deva[लू], @deva[धू], @deva[सू], @deva[खन्], @deva[सह्], and @deva[चर्]; @deva[ऋ]—@deva[अरित्रं] a rudder, helm; an oar; @deva[लवित्रं] a sickle; @deva[धवित्रं] a fan made of the deer's skin; @deva[सवित्रं] cause of generation; @deva[खनित्रं] a spade; @deva[सहित्रं] patience, forbearance; @deva[चरित्रं].

@deva[इन्]—( @deva[इनि], @deva[घिनुण्], @deva[णिनि] )—

@deva[इनि]—is affixed to @deva[जु] with @deva[प्र], @deva[जि], @deva[दृ], @deva[क्षि], @deva[श्रि] with @deva[वि], @deva[वम्], @deva[व्यथ्] with @deva[आ], @deva[अम्] with @deva[अभि], @deva[भू] with @deva[परि] and @deva[सू] with @deva[प्र]; @deva[प्रजविन्] swift-going; @deva[जयिन्] a conqueror; @deva[दरिन्] timid. &c., @deva[क्षयिन्] wasting away; it is also added to @deva[क्री] with @deva[वि] when the noun governed by it is prefixed to it and when the idea of censure or reproach is to be conveyed; @deva[तैलविक्रयी], @deva[सोमविक्रयी], &c.

@deva[घिनुण्]—is affixed to @deva[त्यज्], @deva[रञ्ज्], @deva[भज्], @deva[दुष्], @deva[द्विष्], @deva[द्रुह्], @deva[दुह्], @deva[युज्], @deva[यस्] with @deva[आ], @deva[यस्], @deva[क्रीड्] and @deva[मुष्] with @deva[आ]; @deva[सृ], @deva[दिव्], @deva[क्षिप्], @deva[रट्], @deva[वद्], @deva[दह्], @deva[मुह्], all with @deva[परि]; @deva[सृज्], @deva[पृच्], @deva[ज्वर्], all with @deva[सम्]; @deva[विच्] and @deva[चर्] with @deva[वि]; @deva[लप्], @deva[सृ], @deva[मन्थ्], @deva[वद्], @deva[वस्] all with @deva[प्र]; @deva[चर्] with @deva[अति] and @deva[अप]; @deva[हन्] with @deva[अभि], @deva[रुध्] with @deva[अनु]; and denotes the agent; @deva[त्यज्]—@deva[त्यागिन्] one who abandons, @deva[रागिन्] full of passion, impassioned, a lover; @deva[भागिन्] one who takes a share, @deva[दोषिन्] one who blames; similarly @deva[द्वेषिन्], @deva[द्रोहिन्], &c.; this is also added to @deva[शम्] and the other roots of that group but without occasioning any change in the roots; @deva[शम्]—@deva[शमिन्] tranquil; @deva[मद्]—@deva[मदिन्]; but @deva[मद्] with @deva[उत्] or @deva[प्र]—@deva[उन्मादिन्], @deva[प्रमादिन्].

@deva[णिनि]—is added to the roots of the @deva[ग्रह्] group in the sense of 'the agent;' @deva[गृह्णातीति ग्राहिन्] 'one who takes;' @deva[स्था]—@deva[स्थायिन्], @deva[सि] with @deva[वि]—@deva[विषयिन्] 'a sensualist;' @deva[राध्] with @deva[अप]—@deva[अपराधिन्] 'one who is guilty;' @deva[भू] with @deva[परि]—@deva[परिभाविन्] 'one who defeats;' &c.;—to @deva[हन्] when preceded by @deva[कुमार] and @deva[शीर्ष]; @deva[कुमारं हन्तीति कुमारघातिन्] 'one who murders a child,' @deva[शीर्षघातिन्] 'one who cuts off the head.' This is added to any root, when the subanta other than one denoting a class, precedes it, in the sense of 'in the habit of,' 'disposed to'; @deva[उष्णभोजिन्] (@deva[उष्णं भोक्तुं शीलमस्य]) 'one who eats hot things;' @deva[साधुकारिन्] 'one who acts well;' @deva[ब्रह्मवादिन्] 'one who expounds the Vedas or the nature of Brahman;'—to @deva[मन्] after any subanta. @deva[पण्डितमानिन्] 'one who considers himself a Pandita.' @deva[दर्शनीयमानिन्] 'one who considers himself handsome,' &c.; this is added in the sense of the Past Tense to @deva[यज्] preceded by the name of a sacrifice; @deva[सोमयाजिन्] 'one who has performed the Soma sacrifice;' so @deva[अग्निष्टोमयाजिन्]; and to @deva[हन्] when the noun governed by it is prefixed to it; @deva[पितृव्यघातिन्] 'one who has killed his uncle.' This is also added to a root when a noun signifying a standard of comparison is prefixed to it; @deva[उष्ट्रक्रोशिन्] 'one who utters a sound like that of a camel'; @deva[ध्वांक्षराविन्] 'one who cries like a crow;' this is also added when the observance of a vow is to be indicated; @deva[स्थण्डिलशायिन्] 'one who observes the vow of sleeping on the alter;' also in the sense of 'necessity' or the payment of a debt; @deva[अवश्यंभाविन्] 'what takes place of necessity;' @deva[शतंदायिन्] 'one who pays off a debt of Rs. 100'

@deva[इष्णु]—(@deva[इष्णुच्], @deva[खिष्णुच्]) is added to @deva[कृ] with @deva[अलं] and @deva[निरा], @deva[जन्] with @deva[प्र], @deva[पच्], @deva[पत्] and @deva[मद्] all with @deva[उत्], @deva[रुच्], @deva[त्रप्] with @deva[अप], @deva[वृध्], @deva[सह्], and @deva[चर्] in the sense of 'in the habit of, possessed of the properties of,' or 'expert in' 'acting well;' @deva[अलंकरिष्णु] 'decorating, skilled in decorations; @deva[निराकर्तुं शीलमस्य निराकारिष्णुः] (see Bhaṭṭi. V. 1.) 'repudiating, turning aside,' @deva[उत्पतिष्णु] 'clever in flying up;' @deva[वर्तिष्णु], @deva[वर्धिष्णु], @deva[सहिष्णु], @deva[रोचिष्णु]. &c ; it is found added to some other roots also by poets; e. g @deva[प्रभविष्णु] 'powerful,' @deva[भ्राजिष्णु] 'resplendent,' @deva[क्षयिष्णु], &c

@deva[इष्णु] and @deva[उक]-(@deva[खिष्णुच्], @deva[खुकञ्]) are added to @deva[भू] with the words @deva[आढ्य], @deva[सुभग], @deva[स्थूल], @deva[पलित], @deva[नग्न], @deva[अंध] and @deva[प्रिय] prefixed to it in the sense of @deva[अभूततद्भाव] 'being what a thing or person was not before;' @deva[अनाढ्य आढ्यः संजातः आढ्यंभविष्णु] or—@deva[भावुक] becoming rich not being rich at first, (see Bhaṭṭi. III. 1) so @deva[आढ्यं], @deva[करणम्] &c.

@deva[उ]—(@deva[उ], and @deva[डु])

@deva[उ]—is added to Desiderative bases to form nouns; @deva[चिकीर्षु], desirous of doing; @deva[विजिगीषु] desirous of conquering, &c.; and to @deva[शंस्] with @deva[आ], @deva[भिक्ष्], @deva[विद्], and @deva[इष्]; @deva[आशंसुः] desirous, hopeful. @deva[भिक्षुः] a beggar; @deva[विदुः] one who knows, knowing; @deva[इच्छुः] wishing.

@deva[डु]—is added to @deva[भू] with @deva[वि], @deva[प्र], and @deva[सम्]; @deva[विभुः] all-pervading, mighty, @deva[प्रभुः] able, @deva[संभुः] creating; also to @deva[द्रु]—@deva[मितद्रु] that which moves to a measured distance; @deva[शतद्रुः] which runs in a hundred streams. Name of a river.

@deva[उक]—(@deva[उकञ्])-is affixed to @deva[लष्], @deva[पत्], @deva[पद्], @deva[स्था], @deva[भू], @deva[वृष्], @deva[हन्], @deva[कम्], @deva[गम्], and @deva[शृ] and denotes the agent; @deva[लष्]—@deva[लापुकः] sporting, glittering @deva[पातुकः] falling @deva[भू]—@deva[भावुकः] happening, living; @deva[हन्]—@deva[घातुकः] @deva[कम्]—@deva[कामुकः] amorous.

@deva[उर]—(@deva[कुरच्])-is affixed to @deva[विद्], @deva[भिद्], and @deva[छिद्]; @deva[विदुरः] who knows, knowing;' @deva[भिदुरः] 'breaking, brittle;' @deva[छिदुरः] 'cutting.'

@deva[ऊक]—(@deva[रूक]) is added to @deva[जागृ] and the Fre. Bases of @deva[यज्], @deva[जप्] and @deva[दंश्]; @deva[जागरूक] 'watchful,' &c. (vide Bhaṭṭi. II. 22. Rag. XIV. 85. Sis. XX 36); @deva[पुनः पुनः अतिशयेन वा यजनशीलः]; @deva[यायजूकः] 'one who performs sacrifices frequently' (see Bhaṭṭi. II. 20.); @deva[पुनः पुनः अतिशयेन वा जपतीति जंजपूकः] 'one who mutters prayers repeatedly, an ascetic;' @deva[पुनः पुनः अतिशयेन वा दशतीति दंदशूकः] 'biting frequently, a serpent, demon' (vide Bhaṭṭi I. 26).

@deva[क्विन्], @deva[क्विप्] and @deva[ण्वि]—Derivatives are formed with these affixes which are added to roots and then dropped; the difference between the first two is that in the case of the latter @deva[त्] is inserted between it and the root, if it ends in a short vowel.

@deva[क्विन्]—is affixed to @deva[स्पृश्] preceded by a subanta; @deva[घृतस्पृश्] 'one who touches ghee; @deva[मन्त्रस्पृश्] 'one who touches anything after reciting a holy verse,' &c. except when the subanta means water: @deva[उदकस्पर्शः] 'one who touches water' and not @deva[उदकस्पृश्]. The following words are to be accepted as they are; @deva[यज्]—@deva[ऋत्विज्] (@deva[ऋतौ ऋतौ यजते]) sacrificing regularly at every season; a priest who officiates at a sacrifice; @deva[धृष्]—@deva[दधृष्]—proud, haughty; @deva[सृज्]—@deva[स्रज्] a garland: @deva[दिश्]—@deva[दिश्] a direction; @deva[स्निह्]—@deva[उष्णिह्] name of a metre, words like @deva[प्राचीन] derived from the roots @deva[अञ्च्] and the words @deva[युज्] and @deva[क्रुञ्च्] ought to be considered as derived by means of this affix.

@deva[क्विप्]—this is added to a root with or without any preposition prefixed to it; @deva[सूते असौ सू] or @deva[प्रसूः] one who brings forth, a mother; @deva[सद्]—@deva[द्युसदः] those who sit in heaven, the gods, @deva[द्विष्]—@deva[प्रद्विष्] a powerful enemy; @deva[युज्]—@deva[अश्वयुज्] the constellation of stars called 'Aswini;' @deva[नी]—@deva[सेनानी] the leader of an army; @deva[राज्]—@deva[विराज्] the creator; @deva[चि]—@deva[अग्निचित्] one who consecrates the sacred fire, a householder; @deva[जि]—@deva[इन्द्रजित्] the conqueror of Indra, name of Rāvaṇa's son; @deva[स्तु]—@deva[देवस्तुत्] he who praises the gods; @deva[सु]—@deva[सोमसुत्] the extractor of Soma juice, @deva[कृ]—@deva[कर्मकृत्], @deva[भाषाकृत्], @deva[टीकाकृत्]. &c. This is also added to @deva[दृश्], @deva[स्पृश्], and @deva[सृज्] when the object governed by them is prefixed to them; @deva[सर्वदृश्] seeing all; @deva[मर्मस्पृश्] touching the vitals; @deva[विश्वसृज्] the creator of the universe;—to @deva[अद्] and @deva[हन्]; @deva[क्रव्याद्] a flesh-eater, a demon; @deva[ब्रह्महन्] the Killer of a Brāhmaṇa;—to @deva[छाद्] changed to @deva[छद्]; @deva[तनुच्छद्] a garment. Before this affix roots ending in a nasal lengthen their penultimate; as @deva[शम्]-@deva[प्रशाम्] tranquil; @deva[तन्]-@deva[प्रतान्] one who stretches, &c., except in the case of roots @deva[गम्], @deva[नम्], @deva[यम्], and @deva[तन्], which drop their nasal and then obey the general rule; @deva[अध्वानं गच्छतीति अध्वगत्] a traveller; @deva[परितनोतीति]—@deva[परीतत्] stretching on all sides; @deva[सुनत्] yielding, poor; @deva[संयत्] well restrained, &c ; the @deva[आ] of @deva[शास्] is changed to @deva[इ] before this; @deva[मित्रं शास्तीति]—@deva[मित्रशिष्] one who gives advice to his friend; @deva[आशिष्] a blessing; @deva[गृ] forms @deva[गिर्] speech; the roots @deva[भ्रंस्], @deva[स्रंस्], and @deva[ध्वंस्] drop their nasal and insert @deva[त्] before their final; @deva[वाहभ्रत्] dropping down from a vehicle, @deva[उखास्रत्] dropping down from a vessel; @deva[पर्णध्वत्] falling down from a leaf; before this affix @deva[दिव्] changes its @deva[व्] to @deva[उ] and other roots change their @deva[व्] to @deva[ऊ]; @deva[अक्षद्युत्] (@deva[अक्षैर्दीव्यति]) a gambler; @deva[वे]—@deva[ऊः] a weaver; @deva[अव्]—@deva[ऊः] a protector; this forms Vṛddhi with a preceding @deva[अ]; @deva[जन+ऊ=जनौः] the protector of the people, @deva[ज्वर्]—@deva[जूर्] feverish, @deva[त्वर्]—@deva[तूर्] swift-going; before this affix @deva[च्] or @deva[छ्] following @deva[र्] is dropped; @deva[मूर्छ्]—@deva[मूर्] swooned; @deva[धुर्व्]—@deva[धूर्] hurting, injuring; @deva[अक्षधूर्] what troubles, i. e. presses heavily on the axle of a carriage, hence the cart-load; the following words are irregularly derived; @deva[वच्]—@deva[वाच्] speech, @deva[प्रच्छ्]—@deva[प्राच्छ्] one who asks; @deva[प्रु]-@deva[कटप्रूः] acting by will, name of Shiva, a kind of worm, a gambler; &c; @deva[श्रि]—@deva[श्रीः] wealth; @deva[व्रज्]—@deva[परिव्राज्] an ascetic; @deva[दिव्]—@deva[विद्युत्] lightning; @deva[गम्]—@deva[जगत्] the world; @deva[ध्यै]—@deva[धीः] the intellect.

@deva[ण्वि]—is affixed to @deva[भज्] which lengthens its @deva[अ] before it; @deva[अंशभाज्] one who takes a share; @deva[प्रभाज्] devoted to, worshipping, &c.

@deva[ति]—(@deva[क्तिन्]) forms fem. abstract nouns; @deva[कृ]—@deva[कृति] an act, &c; @deva[स्तु]-@deva[स्तुति] praise; @deva[गम्]-@deva[गति] gait, &c; @deva[रम्]-@deva[रति] sport; @deva[नम्]-@deva[नति] a bow; @deva[स्था]—@deva[स्थिति] state; @deva[गै]—@deva[गीति] a song, &c; @deva[पा]—@deva[पीतिः] drinking; @deva[पच्]—@deva[पक्तिः] cooking; @deva[यज्]—@deva[इष्टिः] a sacrifice, &c. It is added to the roots @deva[श्रु], @deva[त्यज्], @deva[स्तु] and @deva[इष्] in the sense of 'the instrument of'; @deva[श्रुतिः] the instrument of hearing i. e. the ear, &c. To the root @deva[पद्] with @deva[सम्] or @deva[वि], @deva[क्तिन्] or @deva[क्विप्] is added; @deva[सम्पत्तिः] or @deva[सम्पत्], prosperity; @deva[विपत्ति] or @deva[विपद्] adversity; @deva[नि] instead of @deva[ति] is added to roots ending in @deva[ऋ] and to @deva[लू] and others; @deva[कॄ]—@deva[कीर्णिः] scattering. The following words are to be taken as they are:—@deva[सो]—@deva[साति] end; @deva[हन्]—@deva[हेति] a weapon; @deva[कृत्]—@deva[कीर्ति] fame.

@deva[तृ]—(@deva[तृच्], @deva[तृन्])—@deva[तृच्]—is affixed to all roots and denotes the agent; @deva[कृ]-@deva[कर्तृ] a doer; @deva[गम्]-@deva[गन्तृ], @deva[पच्]-@deva[पक्तृ], @deva[सह्]-@deva[सोढृ] or @deva[सहितृ], @deva[इष्]-@deva[एष्टृ] or @deva[एषितृ] &c ; @deva[क्रम्]-@deva[क्रन्तृ] or @deva[क्रान्तृ] or @deva[क्रमितृ] one who goes, &c., @deva[होतृ] 'one habitually sacrificing' (@deva[हु]) &c

@deva[त्र]—@deva[ष्ट्रन्] is added to @deva[दा] or @deva[दो], @deva[नी], @deva[शास्], @deva[यु], @deva[युज्], @deva[स्तु], @deva[तुद्], @deva[सिच्], @deva[मिह्], @deva[पत्], @deva[पद्], @deva[नह्] and @deva[दंश्] and shows the instrument of the action denoted by the root; @deva[दा] or @deva[दो]-@deva[दात्रं] an instrument for cutting, a sickle. @deva[नेत्रं] the instrument of guidance i. e. the eye, @deva[शस्]—@deva[शस्त्रं] a weapon, @deva[शास्]-@deva[शास्त्रं], @deva[यु]-@deva[योत्रं], @deva[युज्]-@deva[योक्त्रं] the rope by which an animal is tied to the pole of a carriage, @deva[स्तु]-@deva[स्तोत्रं] a hymn of praise, @deva[तुद्]-@deva[तोत्रं] a whip, @deva[सिच्]—@deva[सेक्त्रं] a watering pot, @deva[मिह्]—@deva[मेढ्रं], @deva[पत्]—@deva[पत्रं] a vehicle, the wing of a bird, &c. @deva[नह्]—@deva[नध्री] a leather-strap, @deva[दंश्]—@deva[दंष्ट्रा] the jaw; it is also added to—@deva[पू] in the sense given—@deva[पोत्रं] the snout of a hog, a ploughshare, the thunderbolt, a garment;—@deva[पवित्रं] an instrument for purifying, a sort of ring of kusha grass worn on the fourth finger on religious occasions, and to @deva[धे] and @deva[धा], @deva[धात्री] a mother, a foster mother, the earth, name of a tree, Emblic myrobalan.

@deva[त्रिम]—(@deva[क्त्रिम]) is added to a few roots; @deva[पच्]—@deva[पाक्त्रिमः] (@deva[पाकेन निर्वृत्तः]) ripened, matured; @deva[कृत्रिम] artificial from @deva[कृ], @deva[दात्रिमः] produced by gift (see Bhaṭṭi. I 10, 13).

@deva[थक]—@deva[गै]—@deva[गाथकः] a singer.

@deva[न]—(@deva[नङ्], @deva[नन्])—

@deva[नङ्]—is added to @deva[यज्], @deva[याच्], @deva[यत्], @deva[विच्छ्], @deva[प्रच्छ्], and @deva[रक्ष्]; @deva[यज्ञः] a sacrifice, @deva[याच्ञा] beggary, @deva[यत्नः] an effort, @deva[विश्नः] going, lustre, @deva[प्रश्न] a question, @deva[रक्ष्णः] protector.

@deva[नन्]—@deva[स्वप्नः] sleep, a dream.

@deva[नज्]—(@deva[नजिङ्])—is added to @deva[स्वप्], @deva[तृष्], and @deva[धृष्], in the sense of 'in the habit of;' @deva[स्वप्नज्] sleepy, @deva[तृष्णज्] thirsty, @deva[धृष्णज्] bold, confident.

@deva[नु]—(@deva[क्नु])—is added to @deva[त्रस्], @deva[गृध्], @deva[धृष्] and @deva[क्षिप्] in the sense of 'in the habit of;' @deva[त्रस्नु] timid, @deva[गृध्नु] covetous, greedy, @deva[धृष्णु] bold, @deva[क्षिप्नु] throwing, casting.

@deva[मर]—(@deva[क्मरच्])—@deva[सृ]—@deva[सृमर] going, a kind of deer, @deva[घस्]—@deva[घस्मर] and @deva[अद्]—@deva[अद्मर] voracious, gluttonous, glutton.

@deva[य]—(@deva[क्यप्])—is added to @deva[व्रज्], @deva[यज्] and @deva[कृ] and forms fem. abstract nouns; @deva[व्रज्या] asceticism, an attack, @deva[इज्या] a sacrifice, @deva[कृत्या] doing; it also takes @deva[श] and @deva[क्तिन्]; @deva[क्रिया], @deva[कृतिः]; it is affixed to @deva[अज्], (not changed to @deva[वी] in this case) with @deva[सम्], @deva[सद्] and @deva[पत्] with @deva[नि], @deva[मन्], @deva[विद्], @deva[सु], @deva[शी], @deva[भृ] and @deva[इ] in the sense of either the place or the instrument of the action denoted by the roots; @deva[समज्या] assembly, @deva[निषद्या] a couch, a market place, the hall where an assembly meets, @deva[निपत्या] slippery ground, @deva[मन्या] the nape of the neck, @deva[विद्या], @deva[सुत्या] a sprinkling with the Soma juice, @deva[शय्या] a bed, @deva[भृत्या] wages, @deva[इत्या] a vehicle.

@deva[र]—is affixed to @deva[नम्], @deva[कम्प्], @deva[स्मि], @deva[कम्], @deva[हिंस्], and @deva[दीप्]; @deva[नम्र] bowing down, yielding, @deva[कम्प्र] shaking, tremulous, @deva[स्मेर] smiling, @deva[कम्र] desirous, beautiful, @deva[हिंस्र] injurious, murderous, @deva[दीप्र] shining. The word @deva[अजस्रं] adv. is also derived from @deva[जस्] with @deva[न] (changed to @deva[अ]) and @deva[र]

@deva[रु]—is added to @deva[दा], @deva[धे], @deva[सि], @deva[शद्] and @deva[सद्]: @deva[दा]—@deva[दारुः] 'one who gives or eats;' @deva[धे]—@deva[धारुः] 'one who drinks;' @deva[सेरुः] 'one who binds,' @deva[शद्रुः] 'one who goes or destroys;' @deva[सद्रुः] 'one who goes or takes rest.'

@deva[वन्]—(@deva[क्वनिप्])—@deva[पारदृश्वन्] from @deva[दृश्] 'one who has seen the other side, hence, adept in,' @deva[राजयुध्वन्] 'one who has fought with a king'; similarly @deva[राजकृत्वन्], @deva[सहयुध्वन्], and @deva[सहकृत्वन्].

@deva[वर]—(@deva[क्वरप्]) is affixed to the roots @deva[इ], @deva[जि], @deva[नश्] and @deva[सृ]; @deva[इत्वर] going, cruel, @deva[जित्वर] victorious, @deva[नश्वर] perishable, fleeting; it is also added to @deva[गम्]; @deva[गत्वर] transient, going.

## Roots Governing Double Accusative

The roots given in the following Kārikā govern a double Accusative—

@deva[दुह्याच्पच्दण्ड्रुधिप्रच्छिचिब्रूशासुजिमथ्मुषाम् ।]
@deva[कर्मयुक्स्यादकथितं तथा स्यान्नीहृकृष्वहाम् ॥]

i. e. the roots @deva[दुह्] to milk, @deva[पच्] to cook, @deva[दण्ड्] to punish, @deva[रुध्] to obstruct, @deva[प्रच्छ्] to ask, @deva[चि] to collect, @deva[ब्रू] to speak, @deva[शास्] to instruct, @deva[जि] to win (as a wager), @deva[मन्थ्] to churn, and @deva[मुष्] to steal; as also @deva[नी], @deva[हृ], and @deva[कृष्] and @deva[वह्]; and the synonyms of these; @deva[गां दोग्धि पयः] he milks (draws milk from) the cow, @deva[बलिं याचते वसुधां] he begs the earth of Bali; @deva[तण्डुलानोदनं पचति] he cooks rice (into food); similarly @deva[गर्गान् शतं दण्डयति], @deva[व्रजमवरुणद्धि गां], @deva[माणवकं पन्थानं पृच्छति], @deva[वृक्षं अवचिनोति फलानि], @deva[माणवकं धर्मं ब्रूते—शास्ति], @deva[शतं जयति देवदत्तं], @deva[सुधां क्षीरनिधिं मथ्नाति], @deva[देवदत्तं शतं मुष्णाति], @deva[ग्राममजां नयति—हरति—कर्षति—वहति वा]; So @deva[माणवकं धर्मं भाषते—वक्ति वा], @deva[बलिं वसुधां भिक्षते], &c. Vide Bhatti. VI. 8–10

## Eight Gaṇas (Syllabic Feet)

In the case of metres regulated by syllables each line is divided into groups of three syllables each, called Gaṇas or syllabic feet, named as @deva[म], @deva[न], @deva[भ], @deva[य], @deva[ज], @deva[र], @deva[स] and @deva[त]. The names and the Schemes of these are given in the following stanza.

@deva[मस्त्रिगुरुस्त्रिलघुश्च नकारो भादिगुरुः पुनरादिलघुर्यः ।]
@deva[जो गुरुमध्यगतो रलमध्यः सोन्तगुरुः कथितोन्तलघुस्तः ॥]

i. e. @deva[म] has all its syllables long; @deva[न] has all its syllables short; @deva[भ] has its first syllable long, @deva[य] has its first syllable short; @deva[ज] has its middle syllable long; @deva[र] has its middle syllable short; @deva[स] has its last syllable long and @deva[त] has its last syllable short.[^1]

The symbol ⏑ stands for a short or light syllable; the symbol – denotes a long vowel or a heavy syllable. Symbolically represented these Gaṇas will stand as under—

@deva[म] – – –  @deva[ज] ⏑ – ⏑
@deva[न] ⏑ ⏑ ⏑  @deva[र] – ⏑ –
@deva[भ] – ⏑ ⏑  @deva[स] ⏑ ⏑ –
@deva[य] ⏑ – –  @deva[त] – – ⏑

Similarly the letter @deva[ल] is used to denote a short syllable and @deva[ग] a long one at the close of a line.

[^1]: The following verse is easier to remember than one given above; @deva[आदिमध्यावसानेषु यरता यान्ति लाघवम् । भजसा गौरवं यान्ति मनौ तु गुरुलाघवम्]

## Five Mātrā Gaṇas

In the case of metres regulated by syllabic instants each line is divided into groups of four mātrās called the Mātrā Gaṇas; one @deva[मात्रा] or instant is allotted to a short vowel and two to a long one. The mātrā gaṇas are five in number. These may be symbolically represented thus:—

@deva[म] – –  @deva[स] ⏑ ⏑ –  @deva[ज] ⏑ – ⏑  @deva[भ] – ⏑ ⏑  @deva[न] ⏑ ⏑ ⏑ ⏑

## Section II. @deva[अर्धसमवृत्तानि]

or Metres with their alternate quarters similar.

### (1) @deva[उपचित्रम्]

Def. @deva[विषमे यदि सौ सलगा दले भौ युजि भाद्गुरुकावुपचित्रम् ।]

Sch. of G. @deva[स, स, स, ल, ग] (odd quarter).
@deva[भ, भ, भ, ग, ग] (even quarter).

Ex. @deva[मुरवैरिवपुस्तनुतां मुदं हेमनिभांशुकचंदनलिप्तम् ।]
@deva[गगनं चपलामिलितं यथा शारदनीरधरैरुपचित्रम्]

### (2) @deva[अपरवक्त्रम्]

(Sometimes called) @deva[वैतालीयम्]

Def. @deva[अयुजि ननरला गुरुः समे तदपरवक्त्रमिदं नजा जरौ ।]

Sch. of G. @deva[न, न, र, ल, ग,] (odd quarter).
@deva[न, ज, ज, र] (even quarter).

Ex. @deva[स्फुटमधुवेणुगीतिभिस्तमपरवक्त्रमवेत्य माधवम् ।]
@deva[मृगयुवतिगणैः समं स्थिता व्रजवनिता धृतचित्तविभ्रमा ॥]

### (3) @deva[पुष्पिताग्रा]

(also called @deva[औपच्छंदसिक]).

Def. @deva[अयुजि नयुगरेफतो यकारो युजि च नजौ जरगाश्च पुष्पिताग्रा ।]

Sch. of G. @deva[न, न, र, य] (odd quarter).
@deva[न, ज, ज, र, ग] (even quarter).

Ex. @deva[अथ मदनवधूरुपप्लवान्तं व्यसनकृशा परिपालयांबभूव ।]
@deva[शशिन इव दिवातनस्य लेखा किरणपरिक्षययूसरा प्रदोषम् ॥]

### (4) @deva[मालभारिणी]

Def. @deva[विषमे ससजे गुरू नगे नगे नाविषमस्त्रयेण तु मालभारिणीयम् ।]

Sch. of G. @deva[स, स, ज, ग, ग] (odd quarter).
@deva[स, भ, र, य] (even quarter).

Ex. @deva[मुहुरङ्गुलिसंवृताधरोष्ठं प्रतिषेधाक्षरविक्लवाभिरामम् ।]
@deva[मुखमंसविवर्ति पक्ष्मलाक्ष्याः कथमन्युन्नमितं न चुम्बितं तु ॥] S'ak. III. 23.

### (5) @deva[वियोगिनी]

(also called @deva[वैतालीय] or @deva[सुंदरी]).

Def. @deva[विषमे ससजा गुरुः समे सभरा लोऽथ गुरुर्वियोगिनी ।]

Sch. of G. @deva[स, स, ज, ग] (odd quarter).
@deva[स, भ, र, ल, ग] (even quarter).

Ex. @deva[सहसा विदधीत न क्रियामविवेकः परमापदां पदम् ।]
@deva[वृणते हि विमृश्यकारिणं गुणलुब्धाः स्वयमेव संपदः ॥]

### (6) @deva[वेगवती]

Def. @deva[सयुगात्सगुरू विषमे चेद् भाविह वेगवती युजि भाद्रौ ॥]

Sch. of G. @deva[स, स, स, ग] (odd quarter).
@deva[भ, भ, भ, ग] (even quarter).

Ex. @deva[स्मरवेगवती व्रजरामा केशववंशरवैरतिमुग्धा ।]
@deva[रभसान्न गुरून् गणयंती केलिनिकुंजगृहाय जगाम ॥]

### (7) @deva[हरिणप्लुता]

Def. @deva[सयुगात्सलघू विषमे गुरुर्युजि नभौ भरकौ हरिणप्लुता ।]

Sch. of G. @deva[स, स, स, ल, ग] (odd quarter).
@deva[न, भ, भ, र] (even quarter).

Ex. @deva[स्फुटफेनचया हरिणप्लुता बलिमनोज्ञतटा तरणेः सुता ।]
@deva[कलहसकुलारवशालिनी विहरतो हरति स्म हरेर्मनः ॥]

